tor","/prf"]],"story":"<p class=\"prf-lede prf-story\">As of Oct 12, the record here runs from 1951 to 2025, and on the middle value of the county&rsquo;s 9 grids October to November came in under 90% of normal in 42 of 75 years. On the middle of the grids, September to October 2025 got 37% of normal and October to November 2025 got 41%. So far in 2026, March to April came in at 19% of normal on the middle of the grids. Every grid had its driest year in 1954, with grid 14295 down to 58% that year.</p>"}
